========================================================================
RESIDUAL (honest; do not close 2.9)
========================================================================

1. **Walker is still the token IDENT loop.** L175–192 is not
   `c_secret_emit_guard`. Stmt `println` still `c_emit_println` +
   `__sec__` only. Front-door carries alias + dual-path refuse.

2. **print_err / log / fprintf / syslog are not dual-path secret.**
   emit-c scanner-strong; check type-weak; **llvm fail-open**
   (`call @print_err` of the secret payload). Fail-closed compile on
   check ≠ `ERR\tsecret`. Do **not** claim product log sinks In.
   Growing L175 (or feeding lowered args to the guard) is A's land.

3. **Drop-in empty-arg call is an FN.** `c_secret_emit_guard` scans
   C `args` only when `args != ""`. Check/llvm have tokens, not C text.
   Naive `c_secret_emit_guard(env, sid, "", "", "", "")` would skip the
   scanner and **miss** `println(tok)` on check/llvm.

4. **`print` LLVM println-shape** (s71 R2). Check type-fails; C emit is
   not `oo_print_*`; llvm **will print** SECRET. Not a typed API.

5. **`let f = print_err|log`** aborts the shipping host (tcache). Same
   class as 6.1 `env_set` alias. println/eprintln alias still dual-path
   green via the **front-door** (not stmt belt).

6. **Check cache false-OK** (s71 R9). `.ooda-cache/check` is
   cwd-relative; a stale OK for `secret_sink_fail` hid refuse until
   probes used a clean cwd. emit-c/llvm are the honest refuse rails.

7. **Host ELF not rebuilt.** WT secret-before-type is 6.1, not 2.9, and
   would not add print_err to the walker anyway.

8. **Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / `${}` / 2.10 wrappers** — `SECRET_TAINT.oot`.
   `${}` today is STRING (no-FP is correct for 2.9).

